  {
   "say": "If countries were stocks, which one would you buy?"
  },
  {
   "say": "GDP per person, 1960 to 2025.",
   "screen": "GDP per person, *1960* to *2025*",
   "at": "L1",
   "until": "L5-0.2"
  },
  {
   "say": "Then came oil, and the Gulf rockets."
  },
  {
   "say": "Oil boom: Saudi Arabia hits twenty eight thousand dollars in 1981. Bust: nine thousand by 1988."
  },
  {
   "say": "In 1987, Israel passes Saudi Arabia again, and stays above it every year since."
  },
  {
   "say": "In 1960, an Israeli made nine times what an Egyptian made. Today, almost twenty times."
  },
  {
   "say": "Now take out the oil and gas."
  },
  {
   "say": "Iraq loses over forty percent. Saudi Arabia and Qatar, about a quarter. Israel, under half a percent.",
   "screen": "Minus *resource rents*",
   "at": "L7",
   "until": "L9-0.2"
  },
  {
   "say": "Qatar and Israel end up neck and neck."
  },
  {
   "say": "Empires got rich by taking. Oil states, by drilling."
  },
  {
   "say": "Israel, like Singapore and Korea, had no oil. It had people."
  },
  {
   "say": "Drip irrigation, Waze, Mobileye, Iron Dome. Tech is now fifty eight percent of exports."
  },
  {
   "say": "Something from nothing. Israel had no oil. It invested in people. Invest in Israel."
  }
 ],
